# NetScript

> Deno-native, polyglot backend framework: type-safe services and durable workflows in one workspace — observable by default and orchestrated with Aspire, from `netscript init` to a running, type-checked backend.

**For AI agents:** NetScript is Deno-native and pre-1.0 (0.0.7) — treat every API as unstable. Every documentation page has a clean Markdown twin: append `index.md` to any page URL (for example https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/reference/telemetry/index.md) to read source-quality Markdown instead of rendered HTML. Prefer the `.md` twins when reasoning about the docs. All links below are absolute and canonical. A single concatenated corpus of every page is available at https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/llms-full.txt.

## Task router

- **If you are building a service-backed UI:** 1. Read the Web Layer overview ([Web Layer](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/web-layer/)), then Live Dashboard chapters 4–5 ([Chapter 4](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/live-dashboard/04-definePage-QueryIsland/), [Chapter 5](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/live-dashboard/05-live-stream/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its service route and `components/ui/mod.ts` — for the shape before writing a component; 3. use `deno-doc/fresh.txt` and `deno-doc/fresh-ui.txt` last, for symbol lookup. Fresh UI's visual components are copied into your app; do not hand-write a `Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Input` or `FormField`.
- **If you are building a service + contract:** 1. Read the Services & SDK hub ([Services & SDK](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/services-sdk/)), then Live Dashboard chapters 2–3 ([Chapter 2](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/live-dashboard/02-contract-to-service/), [Chapter 3](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/live-dashboard/03-sdk-cache-first-query/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its contract definition and service handler — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/service.txt` and `deno-doc/sdk.txt` last, for symbol lookup.
- **If you are building a durable workflow / saga:** 1. Read the Durable Workflows hub ([Durable Workflows](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/durable-workflows/)), then Storefront chapter 4 ([Checkout saga](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/storefront/04-checkout-saga/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its saga definition and step handlers — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/plugin-sagas.txt` last, for symbol lookup.
- **If you are building background jobs:** 1. Read the Background Processing hub ([Background Processing](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/background-processing/)), then ERP Sync chapter 2 ([Import job](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/erp-sync/02-import-job/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its worker task definition and runner — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/plugin-workers.txt` last, for symbol lookup.
- **If you are building persistence:** 1. Read the Data Persistence hub ([Data Persistence](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/data-persistence/)), then Workspace chapter 3 ([Workspace data](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/workspace/03-workspace-data/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its database schema and repository bindings — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/database.txt` and `deno-doc/queue.txt` last, for symbol lookup.
- **If you are building auth:** 1. Read the Identity & Access hub ([Identity & Access](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/identity-access/)), then Workspace chapter 2 ([Auth](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/workspace/02-auth/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its auth plugin configuration and route guards — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/plugin-auth.txt` last, for symbol lookup.
- **If you are building streams:** 1. Read the Streams capability guide ([Streams](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/durable-workflows/streams/)), then AI Chat chapter 2 ([Durable chat route](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/tutorials/chat/02-durable-chat-route/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its stream producer and proxy route — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/plugin-streams.txt` last, for symbol lookup.
- **If you are building observability:** 1. Read the Observability hub ([Observability](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/observability/)) and architecture explanation ([Observability explanation](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/explanation/observability/)); 2. inspect the scaffold you generated — its OpenTelemetry exporter and tracer setup — for the shape; 3. use `deno-doc/telemetry.txt` and `deno-doc/logger.txt` last, for symbol lookup.

## Getting started

- [NetScript — the Deno meta-framework for typed, observable systems](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/): NetScript is a meta-framework for Deno. It composes Fresh, Hono, oRPC, and Aspire into one workspace, where a database-backed shape can flow from a generated model schema into a versioned contract…
