3:**Declare the API once — as a versioned contract — and the server handler, the typed client, the OpenAPI spec, and the query layer all derive from that one object.** That is this pillar in a sentence. A [service](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/services-sdk/services/) implements the contract; the [SDK](https://rickylabs.github.io/netscript/services-sdk/sdk/) consumes it. Because both sides import the *same* contract object, a renamed field or a changed response shape is a compile error on both ends before it can ship — there is no hand-written client wrapper to keep in sync, and no separate "update the API docs" step.
